2026-06-22 11:48:28,651 | AGENT | AIInnovation Agent received: The client requires an AI solution that assists hospital staff in their daily activities, facilitates access to information, improves the quality of written outputs, and reduces processing and documentation times. The solution must also provide explainability and traceability of its outputs. What AI components and innovation strategy can we propose to meet these requirements?
2026-06-22 11:49:04,265 | INFO | HTTP Request: POST http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/chat "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
2026-06-22 11:49:04,265 | AGENT | AIInnovation Agent answered: We can propose an AI solution that leverages our Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) capabilities, which generate answers from passages retrieved from the client's controlled corpus, providing grounding and explainability. Our core approach ensures that every answer cites the passages it was generated from, enabling traceability.

To facilitate access to information, our solution can utilize hybrid retrieval, including lexical and semantic search, to quickly surface relevant information from internal procedures, care protocols, and applicable regulatory texts. This will help hospital staff efficiently find the information they need, reducing processing times.

For improving the quality of written outputs, we can employ template-guided drafting, which assists in generating high-quality clinical and administrative content, such as discharge summaries, medical reports, and patient letters. Our system can also provide structured extraction capabilities to support tasks like PMSI/ICD-10 coding from clinical notes.

Our innovation strategy involves an iterative approach with the client's experts, starting with corpus selection and curation, followed by retrieval tuning, prompt and template design per use case, and evaluation loops. This collaborative methodology ensures that our solution meets the specific needs of the hospital staff and complies with regulatory requirements.

To address explainability and traceability, we will provide features such as source citations, retrieved passages, retrieval traces, and logging of every interaction for a posteriori audit. Our human oversight workflow is built into the design, where the AI assistant proposes content, and the professional validates it, consistent with HAS guidance.

By leveraging our RAG capabilities, hybrid retrieval, template-guided drafting, and structured extraction, combined with an iterative development approach and a focus on explainability and traceability, we can propose an effective AI solution that meets the client's requirements and supports hospital staff in their daily activities.
